<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Wellesley, 1st Marquess Wellesley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1760–1842</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard Wellesley, 1st Marquess Wellesley (1760–1842), was Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1798 to 1805. An elder brother of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-wellesley-1st-duke-of-wellington">Duke of Wellington</a>, he greatly expanded British power through the subsidiary alliance system, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-anglo-mysore-war">Fourth Anglo-Mysore War</a> that destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> in 1799 and the Second Anglo-Maratha War. He was later British Foreign Secretary and twice Lord Lieutenant of Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-wellesley-1st-marquess-wellesley.jpg" alt="Richard Wellesley, 1st Marquess Wellesley" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lawrence · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Thomas_Lawrence_(1769-1830)_-_Richard_Colley_Wellesley,_Marquess_Wellesley_(1760-1842)_-_RCIN_400643_-_Royal_Collection.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
